      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those specific actions could indeed indicate targeted harassment, especially given the timeline of allergic substitutions, payroll delays, and scheduling changes that have disrupted your work for three weeks. It is important to gather all relevant documentation now, like copies of the emails and notes on upcoming 1:1s, before speaking to HR or management to establish a clear pattern of behavior. However, relying solely on HR reporting can be risky if you fear retaliation, so you might also consider consulting with an employment lawyer to understand your specific protections under company policy or labor law.",
