      "content": "It is unlikely that employers routinely monitor employee digital activity specifically to detect when an individual is seeking legal counsel unless there is an active, whistleblowing investigation already underway. Instead, to protect yourself, strictly avoid discussing your plans or suspicions about being targeted during informal conversations with coworkers, your manager, or HR, as even accidental slips of the tongue could be twisted into evidence against you. Your best course of action is to limit all future communications regarding the situation to written form, such as emails, which create a permanent record of all requests and promises made by the company. If you smell a rat about surveillance, the safest move is to stop any unencrypted digital communication about the issue entirely until you have secured legal advice.",
